# Blender Template Reference
# scripts/blender-template.blend
# This describes the settings for the base Blender scene matching the reference video style.
# Import this as a .blend reference file when generating 3D motion graphics.

## Scene Settings
- Resolution: 1920 x 1080 (X=1920, Y=1080)
- Frame Rate: 24 fps
- Color Management: Standard (not Filmic) — flat colors required
- Background: Cream `#f2ede4`

## Camera
- Type: Perspective
- Focal Length: 35mm (slight depth, not extreme wide)
- Position: (0, -8, 4) looking at origin (0,0,0)
- Clip Start: 0.1m, End: 100m

## Lighting
- Key Light (Sun): Strength 3.0, Color `#fff5e6` (warm white), Angle 30°
- Fill Light (Area): Strength 1.0, Color `#e8dcc8`, Size 3x3
- No environment lighting (World background disabled or pure cream)

## Materials (Pixel / Flat Style)
- All objects use Principled BSDF with:
  - Base Color: exact hex from palette
  - Roughness: 1.0 (fully matte, no shine)
  - Subsurface: 0
  - Metallic: 0
- Pixel mascot: Orange `#ff8c42`, 8-bit style, sharp edges (no smooth shading)

## Render Output
- Format: PNG (RGBA if needed)
- Color: RGBA
- Output path: ./frames/render_%04d.png
- Resolution %: 100
- Post Processing: Denoise off (preserve sharp pixels)
